# Grim Dawn debug overrides - sourced by launch-grimdawn-box64.sh if this file exists.
#
# DELETE THIS FILE to go back to a normal launch. Nothing in the launcher needs undoing.
#
# Run ONE experiment at a time, or you will not know which one moved the needle.
# Alongside each run:   gd-stutter-probe.py 420 /tmp/gd-probe/runN.tsv
#
# THE BASELINE TO BEAT, measured with everything below at its default:
#     14 episodes per 420s, 6.3s total quiet, median episode 400ms
#     during an episode the game runs at ~115 of its usual 220 ms per 100ms window

# --- ALWAYS ON: the instrument ------------------------------------------------
# "compiler" renders the literal text "Compiling shaders..." only while compilation is in
# flight, so its ABSENCE during a spike is a real result, not a missing reading.
export DXVK_HUD=fps,frametimes,compiler,pipelines,version

# --- EXPERIMENT 5 (active): is the freeze a blocked present? ------------------
# The game runs vsync on (syncToRefresh=true) at 60Hz, and DXVK reports
# VK_PRESENT_MODE_FIFO_KHR with 4 images. FIFO blocks until vblank, and a blocked present
# looks exactly like what the probe measured: main thread asleep, CPU halved, GPU idling.
# syncInterval=0 stops the blocking. Expect tearing - that is the point, not a regression.
#   freezes gone -> the stall is in the present path, and vsync/capture is the thing to fix
#   unchanged    -> presentation is innocent too
export DXVK_CONFIG="dxgi.syncInterval = 0"

# --- ELIMINATED, kept so nobody re-runs them ---------------------------------
#
# EXPERIMENT 2 - box64 dynarec contention. RULED OUT, and it was slightly WORSE:
#   20 episodes vs the baseline 14, and median CPU rose 220->240 ms because the
#   interpreter is slower than translated code. The launcher's comment claiming WAIT=1
#   "avoids the input-thread stall" is therefore stale - WAIT was never the mechanism.
# export BOX64_DYNAREC_WAIT=0
#
# EXPERIMENT 3 - DXVK compiler threads crowding the 10 fast cores. NOT WORTH RUNNING:
#   the state cache grew ZERO times across 420s, and cgroup CPU pressure held at 0.2%.
#   Nothing is being compiled and nothing is being starved.
# export DXVK_NUM_COMPILER_THREADS=4

# --- STILL UNTESTED ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# EXPERIMENT 4 - is the pad involved at all? Play with the controller unplugged, mouse only.
#   The original symptom was pad-specific and this has never actually been tested.
#
# EXPERIMENT 6 - is it the STREAM rather than the game? Sunshine captures 3840x1080 with
#   NvFBC into hevc_nvenc, and its log shows "the capture session must be recreated" errors
#   that tear down capture AND encoder - though none during the runs measured so far.
#   A stream hitch is indistinguishable from a game freeze from where you are sitting.
